<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Config:etc/system_file.xsd">
    <system>
        <tab id="basicrum" translate="label" sortOrder="100">
            <label>Basicrum</label>
        </tab>
        <section id="basicrum" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="900"
                 showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
            <label>Basicrum Analytics</label>
            <tab>basicrum</tab>
            <resource>BasicRum_Analytics::basicrum_analytics</resource>
            <group id="general" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="10"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>General Settings</label>
                <comment>Basicrum emits no storefront monitoring scripts unless it is enabled and the effective Beacon Endpoint and Brum Site ID are valid.</comment>
                <field id="logo" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="0"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <frontend_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\Logo</frontend_model>
                    <label>Basicrum Logo</label>
                    <comment>This field displays the Basicrum logo.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Enable Basicrum</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>New installations are disabled. Enabling still requires valid identity settings below.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="monitoring_status" translate="label" type="note" sortOrder="15"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Monitoring Status</label>
                    <frontend_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\Status</frontend_model>
                </field>
                <field id="beacon_endpoint" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Beacon Endpoint</label>
                    <backend_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Model\System\Config\Backend\BeaconEndpoint</backend_model>
                    <comment>Valid HTTP or HTTPS collector URL without embedded credentials or a fragment. Endpoint query strings remain supported. Required when Basicrum is enabled. HTTP is upgraded to HTTPS unless the explicit development exception is enabled.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="brum_site_id" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Brum Site ID</label>
                    <backend_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Model\System\Config\Backend\BrumSiteId</backend_model>
                    <comment>UUIDv4 copied from the Basicrum backoffice. Required when Basicrum is enabled.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="boomerang_version" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Boomerang Version</label>
                    <frontend_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\BoomerangVersion</frontend_model>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="consent" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Visitor Consent</label>
                <comment>Basicrum does not show a consent banner or persist its own consent decision. Connect your site's consent tool with both public callbacks when consent is required.</comment>
                <field id="enabled" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Require Consent Before Monitoring</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Yes keeps Boomerang unloaded until an allow callback on each page. No starts monitoring immediately; choose No only when deliberate and permitted.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Consent Tool Connection</label>
                    <source_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Block\Adminhtml\System\Config\ConsentMode</source_model>
                    <comment>Phase 1 supports manual callbacks. The currently effective legacy value remains visible for compatibility, but other legacy modes cannot be newly selected and none implies an allow decision.</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
                <field id="integration_help" translate="label" type="note" sortOrder="30"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Manual Callback API</label>
                    <comment><![CDATA[
                        Call <code>window.OPT_IN_BASICRUM_LOADER_WRAPPER()</code> only after your consent tool authoritatively allows performance monitoring on the current page. Call <code>window.OPT_OUT_BASICRUM_LOADER_WRAPPER()</code> for denial, expiry, or withdrawal. A denial before loading may be followed by allow on the same page. After withdrawal during download or after initialization, reload before re-granting. Calls made before the footer loader registers these functions are not queued.
                    ]]></comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="enabled">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="privacy" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="30"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Privacy</label>
                <field id="strip_query_string" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Strip Query Strings</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>When enabled, complete query strings in page, navigation, referrer, and resource URLs are replaced with ?qs-redacted before beacons are sent. URL paths remain.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="performance" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="40"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Performance</label>
                <field id="wait_after_onload" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Wait After Onload</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Delay the page-load beacon after onload. Disabled by default.</comment>
                </field>
                <field id="delay_ms" translate="label comment" type="text" sortOrder="20"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Delay (milliseconds)</label>
                    <validate>validate-number validate-zero-or-greater</validate>
                    <backend_model>BasicRum\Analytics\Model\System\Config\Backend\WaitMilliseconds</backend_model>
                    <comment>Zero disables the delay. Values are bounded to 30000 milliseconds (30 seconds).</comment>
                    <depends>
                        <field id="wait_after_onload">1</field>
                    </depends>
                </field>
            </group>
            <group id="developer" translate="label" type="text" sortOrder="50"
                   showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                <label>Developer</label>
                <field id="development_mode" translate="label comment" type="select" sortOrder="10"
                       showInDefault="1" showInWebsite="1" showInStore="1">
                    <label>Allow HTTP Beacon Endpoint</label>
                    <source_model>Magento\Config\Model\Config\Source\Yesno</source_model>
                    <comment>Development-only exception for local testing. Keep disabled on production stores so HTTP endpoints are upgraded to HTTPS.</comment>
                </field>
            </group>
        </section>
    </system>
</config>
